OL,3,GNEWSA'We have to find a cure for
OL,4,AHuntington's disease'
OL,5,
OL,6,FRomy Kerschbaumer was 48 when her life
OL,7,Fchanged forever after she started
OL,8,Fgetting symptoms of Huntington's
OL,9,Fdisease.
OL,11,FShe was forced to medically retire from
OL,12,Fthe job she "absolutely loved" setting
OL,13,FIT strategy for a government department
OL,14,Fin Jersey.
OL,16,FHuntington's disease relentlessly kills
OL,17,Fbrain cells and resembles a combination
OL,18,Fof dementia, Parkinson's and motor
OL,19,Fneurone disease.
OL,23,APub: 18-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
